The rewrite keeps the same logic. It reads `type` and `profile` into locals, which avoids reloading the members. It also marks the explicit-type path as the likely branch. I have not timed this version, so any speedup is expected rather than measured. Return values are unchanged for every input.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const auto* p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields), 0))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```